{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers","id":769802,"title":"A Few Questions About Chambers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-20T00:36:51-08:00","id":769802,"title":"A Few Questions About Chambers","content":"How exactly do Chambers work?<br /> <br /> The rulebook says that the Chamber has to resonate with both your Legend and the Primordial Dream. Okay. Right. It then specifies exactly how a chamber qualifies to be included, which depends entirely on its connection to the Primordial Dream and, as far as I can tell, has nothing to do with your legend. Unless it having at least one element that matches one of your Lair traits counts? But given that you can create said element pretty easily (e.g.: for Darkness, go in at night and turn off the lights, block the windows if necessary), this doesn't seem like much of a limitation. But whatever.<br /> <br /> Then there's a Wits + Occult + Lair roll which... can tell you more about the potential Chamber? Except you don't appear to need to succeed on the roll to add the Chamber to your Lair. You just spent a point of Satiety and if it meets the relevant requirements, it's yours. And there's a chart with dice mods that gives you more dice for certain conditions, among which are &quot;if you actually investigate what happened to cause the Chamber and find the people involved in the incident that created the Chamber.&quot; So assuming none of the other bonuses apply, if you've actually done your homework enough to get the dice bonus from doing your homework, the dice bonus is worthless because you've already done the homework you need to be able to add the place to your Lair. If you haven't done your research the dice bonus for having met the mortal who lost integrity or the supernatural creature that made them lose it would be very helpful, but you can only GET that dice bonus by doing the things you would need to do in order to be able to add the place to your lair anyways. Which makes me wonder why they are even present as modifiers on the chart.<br /> <br /> Next question: Are Chambers basically just dream-versions of the actual physical locations they are based on? Can you customize them?<br /> If a mortal lost integrity in a spooky graveyard while you were there and it has an environmental commonality with one of your Lair traits and you add it to your Lair as a Chamber, is that Chamber then just a copy of the Graveyard modified as necessary by your other Lair traits? Or could you choose to represent that graveyard as, for example, a black marble path lined by gravestones through the middle of a vast grove of bone-white skeletal trees with grey-scale leaves that rise like gnarled claws out of the earth, each one shackled to the ground with heavy iron chains, with still more chains strung between the trees in a vast iron web and the only sounds the forlorn sighing of the wind rustling the colorless leaves, and the the slight jangling of the web of chains, with your Lair traits being represented as some natural aspect of the environment? <br /> (Toxic, for example, could be represented in this environment as &quot;touching the trees causes every part of them you touched with your flesh to crumble like ash, and dozens of tiny white spiders swarm out of the interior in response to the attack...&quot;, at which point the Toxic tilt starts hitting the intruders in the form of horrible spider bites that necrotize the flesh.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 11-20-2015, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:20:55-08:00","id":770012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers#post769802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rulebook says that the Chamber has to resonate with both your Legend and the Primordial Dream. Okay. Right. It then specifies exactly how a chamber qualifies to be included, which depends entirely on its connection to the Primordial Dream and, as far as I can tell, has nothing to do with your legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that your character is adding it to their Lair and was qualified to do so is the bulk of the connection to their Legend, particularly given the limitations on how many Chambers you can add to the Lair and how often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there's a Wits + Occult + Lair roll which... can tell you more about the potential Chamber? Except you don't appear to need to succeed on the roll to add the Chamber to your Lair. </div> </div> </div>You need to know what happened and what monster made the Chamber before you can incorporate it into the Lair and the roll gives you a couple of hints.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So assuming none of the other bonuses apply, if you've actually done your homework enough to get the dice bonus from doing your homework, the dice bonus is worthless because you've already done the homework you need to be able to add the place to your Lair. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's generally what happens when you skip the typical starting point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you haven't done your research the dice bonus for having met the mortal who lost integrity or the supernatural creature that made them lose it would be very helpful, but you can only GET that dice bonus by doing the things you would need to do in order to be able to add the place to your lair anyways. Which makes me wonder why they are even present as modifiers on the chart. </div> </div> </div>&quot;It is dramatically easier to investigate the formation of a Chamber whose creation involved people who you are even remotely acquainted with&quot; is an incentive to STs to have freestanding Chambers affect the periphery of Beast characters' lives. I'm not sure why you would think the only context in which your character would have met someone whose Integrity-loss formed a Chamber would be in preemptively investigating them for this information \u2014 &quot;I had a run-in with a monster and suffered a freakout&quot; isn't something most mortals share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:08:45-08:00","id":770187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770012#post770012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you would think the only context in which your character would have met someone whose Integrity-loss formed a Chamber would be in preemptively investigating them for this information</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not the only context, but certainly the most likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I had a run-in with a monster and suffered a freakout&quot; isn't something most mortals share. </div> </div> </div>Er, why wouldn't they? I would.<br /> <br /> If I had a clear and unambiguous run-in with a monster that could not be explained away as a person in a costume or something similar, then there are basically two possibilities: one, I hallucinated. Vivid hallucinations are probably a bad sign, and I should immediately go to the doctor and make sure nothing is extremely wrong with me. Depending on the nature of the hallucination, it could be a sign of anything from the relatively benign if frightening sleep paralysis to full blown psychosis. Either way, I want to know. Sure, I could end up in an institution in a worst case scenario, but if I'm suffering from a mental illness bad enough to make me a danger to myself and others, then I probably belong in one. Or it could be the second possibility: monsters are real. Of the two possibilities, &quot;monsters are real&quot; has the burden of proof. Assuming it can meet that burden (which will require tangible evidence beyond the inherently unreliable system of human memory, else we are back to &quot;I probably hallucinated&quot;), then I'm going to be trying to find out everything I can about those monsters. Which will likely involve talking to people about my experience. ... which, given the setup of the World of Darkness means I probably end up dead or worse, but hey, if I knew enough to know that going in, I wouldn't be in a position of having to find out about monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 11-20-2015, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:22:11-08:00","id":770244,"title":"","content":"It's not so much a &quot;research&quot; task, as much as a &quot;Spidey-sense tingling!&quot; task. The roll is an instant action, after all. I don't know where your getting these research bonuses from, but in the Backer pdf, it's less that you've chased down a rumour, more that you found a lingering trace of magic that feels close to your own nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:35:27-08:00","id":770256,"title":"","content":"Research comes in when it wasn't a chamber you were responsible for or present for the creation of. You have to learn what happened and what kind of supernatural creature was responsible. Meeting the mortal it happened to and the supernatural creature who made it happen give you huge bonuses on your roll to know what happened. Which I suppose could theoretically be a mortal or a supernatural being you are already familiar with. Such a coincidence strains my credulity and damages my suspension of disbelief -- especially if it happens in a very large city, though not as bad if the setting is a small town -- but would be a situation in which you could actually use these bonuses without obviating their usefulness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:51:00-08:00","id":770265,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, you're a sort of swamp monster, right? Bob had to to go Gauru down by the pond last week and a fisherman totally wigged out. Might be a decent chamber there for you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T17:01:36-08:00","id":770381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770256#post770256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Research comes in when it wasn't a chamber you were responsible for or present for the creation of. You have to learn what happened and what kind of supernatural creature was responsible. Meeting the mortal it happened to and the supernatural creature who made it happen give you huge bonuses on your roll to know what happened. Which I suppose could theoretically be a mortal or a supernatural being you are already familiar with. Such a coincidence strains my credulity and damages my suspension of disbelief -- especially if it happens in a very large city, though not as bad if the setting is a small town -- but would be a situation in which you could actually use these bonuses without obviating their usefulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>But none of that is necessary to add or access the Chamber, beyond checking to see whether the Horror likes it, for which really only dramatic failure matters. It's about learning what happened, or finding new targets for Inflicting Nightmares,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T18:26:52-08:00","id":770429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770265#post770265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey, you're a sort of swamp monster, right? Bob had to to go Gauru down by the pond last week and a fisherman totally wigged out. Might be a decent chamber there for you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that can work if you are comfortable with other creatures knowing where your Chambers are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770381#post770381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But none of that is necessary to add or access the Chamber, beyond checking to see whether the Horror likes it, for which really only dramatic failure matters. It's about learning what happened, or finding new targets for Inflicting Nightmares,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm getting that. <br /> <br /> What about the other question? Does a Chamber in your Lair have to be a one-to-one representation of the location you created it from, or can you reskin it? If you can reskin it, how similar does it have to be? Silent Hill Otherworld? Or could you have Chambers as environments straight out of the Middlemarches, or Malfeas, or the Underworld so long as they in some way reflect either the original space or the idea of the event that caused a human to fail the SAN check that originally created the Chamber?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T20:22:37-08:00","id":770483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770187#post770187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not the only context, but certainly the most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the most likely context is &quot;someone you know lost Integrity through an encounter with the supernatural.&quot;<br /> <br /> If &quot;you can more easily learn about the circumstances that generated a Chamber if any of its subjects were part of your personal experience and those subjects do not necessarily volunteer that information without prompting&quot; strains your credulity, I'm not sure what you expected out of this game where narrative and fatalism are pervasive concepts and the supernatural is hidden largely because people don't like what happens when they acknowledge it too regularly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Er, why wouldn't they? I would. </div> </div> </div>Your likelihood of being a PC in the World of Darkness does not mean every mortal character shares your enthusiasm for sticking their arm into the viper pit that is the greater supernatural world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I had a clear and unambiguous run-in with a monster that could not be explained away as a person in a costume or something similar, </div> </div> </div>Stopping the paragraph here, because you're adding a qualifier that is not necessary. The character has to have 1) lost Integrity 2) in an encounter with the supernatural. There's nothing in there about clear and unambiguous; the terror is the thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or it could be the second possibility: monsters are real. Of the two possibilities, &quot;monsters are real&quot; has the burden of proof. Assuming it can meet that burden (which will require tangible evidence beyond the inherently unreliable system of human memory, else we are back to &quot;I probably hallucinated&quot;), then I'm going to be trying to find out everything I can about those monsters. Which will likely involve talking to people about my experience. ... which, given the setup of the World of Darkness means I probably end up dead or worse, but hey, if I knew enough to know that going in, I wouldn't be in a position of having to find out about monsters. </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, you do your best to avoid contact with the person you think is a monster until they go away, because incidental contact with the supernatural categorically does not get better from you picking at it without grossly disproportionate luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T21:05:13-08:00","id":770506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770187#post770187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, why wouldn't they? I would.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T23:01:42-08:00","id":770552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770429#post770429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm getting that.<br /> <br /> What about the other question? Does a Chamber in your Lair have to be a one-to-one representation of the location you created it from, or can you reskin it? If you can reskin it, how similar does it have to be? Silent Hill Otherworld? Or could you have Chambers as environments straight out of the Middlemarches, or Malfeas, or the Underworld so long as they in some way reflect either the original space or the idea of the event that caused a human to fail the SAN check that originally created the Chamber?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would necessarily be colored by the Lair Traits present when the Chamber was accessed, so, for example, a building that was added as a Chamber that used the Flooded trait as a catalyst will always display some evidence of flooding, regardless of whether the trait is active, be it in the form of shallow standing water, or water-logged wall panels, etc.<br /> <br /> If you were to find a locale in another plane of existence where the other requirements are met, you could have a Chamber designed after another Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T23:10:10-08:00","id":770556,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the World of Darkness is colder, harsher, and more sinister than the real world. Between various and sundry Supernatural plots that require Humanity to stay in the dark, those require human fuel to function, and the mere possibility that there are in fact organizations that benefit from actively silencing bystanders via death or imprisonment, odds are you'd never survive long enough to speak to another living soul about your experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T10:02:43-08:00","id":770810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769802-a-few-questions-about-chambers?p=770552#post770552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would necessarily be colored by the Lair Traits present when the Chamber was accessed, so, for example, a building that was added as a Chamber that used the Flooded trait as a catalyst will always display some evidence of flooding, regardless of whether the trait is active, be it in the form of shallow standing water, or water-logged wall panels, etc.<br /> <br /> If you were to find a locale in another plane of existence where the other requirements are met, you could have a Chamber designed after another Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, going off of the available information and the comparative precedent of Chantries and Golden Roads (and also extrapolating from the fact that opening a Primordial Pathway only lasts for a few turns normally), creating a Burrow may generate logically-necessary components for a bridge in an appropriate spot within the Chamber \u2014 a door or alleyway that doesn't exist in the real location needn't exist at the periphery of the Chamber's replica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}